WEBVTT


00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.633
- Morning, Ms. Rita.
- Morning, Monty.


00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.239
- Hey, Maya.
- Hey, Monty.


00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.501
Hey, baby.


00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.372
- What up, Willie?
- What's up, young blood?


00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.275
- How are you?
- Old and tired, man.


00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:12.814
- That woman say this engine won't start.
- Yeah. Well, it won't.


00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.910
You know, Monty,
he was supposed to fix it.


00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.682
He never did.


00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.019
He don't know what he doing.
That fool can't even see.


00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.218
I saw your mama the night you was made.


00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.490
What you say to me?
Don't make me put this baby down.


00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.962
And that ain't no way to talk to me.


00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.033
I gave this car service
one of its best clients.


00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.261
- Yeah. You never let me forget it, neither.
- That's right.


00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.031
- Maya, I'll look at it for you, baby.
- Thank you.


00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.435
Take a seat.


00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.563
You all right?


00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.733
And you better do something,
you know Chico quit.


00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.243
You're gonna lose my boss as a client.


00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.212
- Here you go, boy.
- How much is here?


00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.513
Well, not enough, but I'll get it to you.
I promise, okay?


00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.982
Hey, man, look,
I just lost one of my drivers.


00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:56.425
He was the only one classy enough to drive
one of them corporate types, you know.


00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.621
Now, listen to me.


00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.358
No, no, no, Willie. You know
I can't stand them stuck-up types.


00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.899
Hear me out. It pays good.


00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.491
Oh, come on now.


00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:06.436
It will help you make more
of a down payment for this place.


00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.439
Man, Willie, you know
I'm better under the hood


00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.872
than I am behind the wheel, man.


00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:13.036
Do you really wanna buy this place?
Now this is a start.


00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.273
Pay is good. Now she's a good client.


00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.042
And she pays well. I don't want to lose her.


00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.708
- I'll think about it.
- You'll think what?


00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.513
- I'll think about it.
- What?


00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.645
- Watch it, old man.
- You watch it.


00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.484
Maya, turn the key.


00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:33.623
- Thank you, Monty.
- All right, baby.


00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.264
You know, this should really be your place.


00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.305
Oh, it will be soon, baby. All right.


00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:24.414
- Hey, boy. How you been?
- What up, Kevin?


00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.950
You all right?


00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.952
Amen, amen.


00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:31.490
Wilbert, get up.


00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:32.922
- Hey, Monty.
- Hey, Ms. Rochelle.


00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.390
You got people stepping all over you.


00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:35.620
- Get up.
- He at it again?


00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.491
Always. Always.


00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.394
Hi, Monty.


00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:42.263
Wilbert. Get up, boy.


00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.835
Anybody home?


00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:46.268
Sierra, get the door.


00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:56.272
- Who is it?
- Who is it? It's your daddy. Open up.


00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.577
- Hey, y'all. It's Daddy.
- Daddy.


00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:01.118
Come on, y'all. Hurry up.


00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:05.653
What up? Come here.
Come here. Come here.


00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:08.249
What's going on? Can I get in?


00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.923
Hey, Ms. Katheryn.


00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.957
- Hey, Daddy. What did you bring us?
- Now, is that all I'm good for?


00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.501
- No, Daddy.
- Can I get some love?


00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.296
Daddy, you know
I got a B on my class project?


00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:23.602
- Thanks for helping me.
- What did I tell you?


00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.234
That I was gonna get a good grade
and I did.


00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:28.711
Hey, Daddy, will you take us
to the movies this weekend?


00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:29.839
No.


00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.448
Okay.


00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.213
I'll take you out to the movies.


00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.016
You know Saturday
is Daddy-daughter day, so...


00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.422
- Okay. So, Daddy, what did you bring us?
- Just some food, baby.


00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:44.362
That always comes in handy.


00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.425
You girls go in the room.
Let me to talk to your daddy.


00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.364
Yeah, get in there.
Don't let me come in there.


00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.733
What y'all doing? Playing checkers, huh?


00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:53.829
Y'all been playing something.


00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.033
Thanks, Katheryn.


00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:59.771
$200, this week.


00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.711
I'll bring the rest to you.


00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:07.075
You know, Ms. Kat, you know
you got to take care of that cough.


00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:11.350
I mean, it sounds like it's getting worse
every time I come up in here.


00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:12.515
Yeah.


00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:16.821
- Jenny been by?
- That daughter of mine?


00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.593
No, only time I see her
is when she's driving by.


00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.999
She ain't been here
to see these girls in months.


00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:28.130
So happy you're here, or they wouldn't
know they had a daddy or a mama.


00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:32.967
Monty, listen.


00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:34.676
Sit down.


00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:36.446
What's wrong?


00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:44.887
I need you to go down
to family court with me right away


00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:47.721
so you can tell them
that you're taking the girls.


00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.658
I need you to raise them.


00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:52.356
Ms. Kat, you know I love my kids,
but I can't take them full time.


00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:54.490
Well, then they're gonna have to stay
with their mama.


00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.034
- Now, you know I don't want that.
- Neither do I.


00:08:57.136 --> 00:09:01.095
Especially since she living with that Joe,
the biggest drug dealer in the area.


00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:05.041
Sitting up there in that window
staring down at all of us like he's God.


00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.239
And she's right there with him.


00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:11.476
She don't care about nobody but herself.


00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:15.543
Do you know what'll happen to them girls
if they have to live with their mama, huh?


00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.156
God forbid.


00:09:19.292 --> 00:09:22.261
- Monty, please.
- Ms. Kat, I...


00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:24.295
I have lung cancer.


00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:29.133
I am dying, Monty.


00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:33.604
I've been hanging in there for them girls
as long as I can, but I'm tired.


00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:36.305
I'm tired.


00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:44.341
Why didn't you say something?
Why didn't you tell me this?


00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.560
Ms. Kat, it's gonna be all right.


00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:59.028
It is not gonna be all right.


00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:35.964
Why didn't y'all call me?


00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:37.626
- Mommy!
- Don't look at her.


00:10:37.737 --> 00:10:39.261
No, wait.
Wait, where do you think you're going?


00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:42.603
These are my kids.
Stop. Stop. Get into the car, baby.


00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:44.972
- Stop. Quit it.
- No, you get off of me.


00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:47.443
Stop it, Jenny. Stop it.


00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:50.413
- Everything all right, baby?
- No, you get my kids out of this car.


00:10:50.516 --> 00:10:52.950
Jenny, stop it now. Jenny, stop. Stop.


00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:55.145
You have not been
to see these kids in months.


00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:57.449
- You want to come take them now?
- Get your hands off of me.


00:10:57.556 --> 00:10:58.921
You got to be crazy. Get out of here.


00:10:59.025 --> 00:11:02.051
- Now, you need back up, son.
- Yo, do me a favor, shut up.


00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:05.289
- Do me a favor, dawg, just hold it.
- Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!


00:11:05.398 --> 00:11:07.491
Go ahead, baby. Go ahead.
Put your seatbelt on. It's okay.


00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.124
This is your mother's funeral.


00:11:09.235 --> 00:11:12.204
And you know
she wanted these girls to go with him.


00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:14.169
Jennifer, you know it.


00:11:14.273 --> 00:11:16.264
You out whoring around with these thugs.


00:11:16.375 --> 00:11:18.866
She didn't want these girls
around all of this foolishness.


00:11:18.978 --> 00:11:20.639
Let me tell you something, Aunt Rita.


00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:23.909
All right, these are my kids.
Do you hear me?


00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:26.416
You ain't just gonna take them from me.


00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:29.147
And let me tell you,
you go make your mechanic money,


00:11:29.255 --> 00:11:32.281
you save it 'cause we going to court.
You hear me?


00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:35.519
Give me my kids back.
You're gonna give them back to me.


00:11:38.297 --> 00:11:40.026
You stay out of my way.


00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.464
- What are you doing?
- Think you gonna let my mama die?


00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:43.899
Calm down. Come on, calm down.


00:11:44.003 --> 00:11:47.234
You gonna let them bury my mama
and you don't tell me, Wilbert?


00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.068
- You should've been there for your mama.
- That's right.


00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:51.143
- You know it ain't right.
- It's too late now.


00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.540
Daddy, you know this place
is too small for all of us.


00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:58.014
- We don't have anywhere else to go.
- We can go live with Mama.


00:11:58.117 --> 00:12:00.608
China, Mama don't want us. She never did.


00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.621
- That is not true.
- It is true.


00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:06.453
- Is that true, Daddy?
- I'll tell you what is true.


00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:08.857
I want you all to come stay with me.


00:12:08.961 --> 00:12:10.519
Where are we gonna sleep?


00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:13.826
Well, I'm gonna sleep on the couch
and you guys,


00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:16.458
I mean girls,
are gonna sleep in the bedroom.


00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:20.166
I fixed it up.


00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:22.137
How bad was it before?


00:12:23.976 --> 00:12:26.137
Daddy, China pees in the bed.


00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:27.872
And I ain't sleeping with her.


00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.072
I do not.


00:12:29.181 --> 00:12:31.376
Why I got to put up
with being insulted like that?


00:12:31.484 --> 00:12:33.008
- What's wrong with you?
- Whatever.


00:12:33.119 --> 00:12:35.815
We need some separate beds
or some bunk beds or something


00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:38.219
- 'cause this ain't gonna work.
- Well, I'll work on it, okay?


00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:41.122
Well, while you work on it,
how about feeding us?


00:12:41.227 --> 00:12:43.855
And getting all three of us some food?
'Cause all three of us are hungry.


00:12:43.963 --> 00:12:45.863
You know what?
You got a mouth like your mama.


00:12:45.965 --> 00:12:49.696
You need to put your clothes
in them drawers right here. Thank you.


00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:51.565
I like this bedroom.


00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:08.381
Lord, how am I gonna do this?


00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.462
Man, I can't believe I'm doing this.


00:13:23.569 --> 00:13:25.730
You waiting for Ms. Rossmore?


00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:31.204
Yeah. Rossmore. Julia Rossmore.


00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:34.442
Good luck.


00:13:35.114 --> 00:13:37.241
What do you mean, "Good luck"?


00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.976
- Good day, Ms. Rossmore.
- Good morning.


00:13:49.128 --> 00:13:52.894
- You gonna open the door?
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:01.102
- Can you close the door?
- Yeah.


00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:06.940
What you laughing at?


00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.280
Tell him to meet me there.
Tell him to wait then.


00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:21.721
I'm surprised
the jury has returned so soon, myself.


00:14:21.827 --> 00:14:25.854
No, it's a great thing. Yeah, definitely.
All right, see you in a second.


00:14:27.099 --> 00:14:29.465
Did they tell you I need you to be on call?


00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:35.073
- Oh, you talking to me?
- You're the only other person in the car.


00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:38.234
Oh, no. You know what? I thought
you were still on the phone, you know.


00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:43.213
Well, basically, all I need you to do
is get me to the office and get me to court.


00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:44.509
Sometimes I work late.


00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:47.051
And sometimes I entertain clients
after work, that sort of thing.


00:14:47.152 --> 00:14:50.349
You know what, Ms. Rossmore? Right now
I need all the overtime I can get so...


00:14:50.456 --> 00:14:52.356
- I'm sorry. What's your name?
- Monty.


00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:56.155
Monty. Look, I don't like to fraternize so
let's keep this strictly professional. Okay?


00:14:56.262 --> 00:14:57.923
- Yes, ma'am.
- Fabulous.


00:15:07.973 --> 00:15:09.270
Excuse me.


00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:11.905
I'm sorry about that.


00:15:23.422 --> 00:15:25.754
Are you... Am I getting punked?


00:15:26.692 --> 00:15:29.183
No, you're not getting punked, ma'am.


00:15:29.295 --> 00:15:31.490
I just, you know,
thought you might want the radio on.


00:15:31.597 --> 00:15:33.531
- No, I like silence.
- Yes, ma'am.


00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:34.792
Silence.


00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.266
You've missed your turn.
I asked you to take the freeway.


00:15:37.369 --> 00:15:38.802
Well, you know what?
This way is much faster.


00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:39.962
Excuse me?


00:15:40.072 --> 00:15:42.336
Yeah. You seem like you're in a rush
and this way is faster, so...


00:15:42.441 --> 00:15:44.466
Yeah, I am in a rush and I know this city!


00:15:44.576 --> 00:15:47.340
The freeway would have bypassed
all of this lunchtime traffic.


00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:48.845
I cannot believe this.


00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:52.475
- Why are you stopping?
- Because we're here now.


00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:01.722
- Next time follow my instructions, okay?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.160
Ms. Rossmore.


00:16:09.268 --> 00:16:12.032
The jury has a question
that they need answered.


00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:14.799
They want to know if
the damage award can be higher


00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:17.569
- than what was previously requested.
- Well, Your Honor...


00:16:17.676 --> 00:16:19.507
How's the driving going?


00:16:19.611 --> 00:16:22.102
Oh, look, she is something else.


00:16:22.214 --> 00:16:24.739
I know. I've worked for her four years.


00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:28.843
She's good though. She wins every case.
And this is a big one.


00:16:29.822 --> 00:16:31.255
Settlement.


00:16:32.191 --> 00:16:34.591
That means she just won a grip of money.


00:16:34.693 --> 00:16:36.354
She's that good?


00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:38.259
My client's willing to talk.


00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:41.765
Oh, and she's also impatient.
So you might want to get out to the car.


00:16:55.614 --> 00:16:57.445
Sorry about that.


00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:03.316
Your Honor, the people have no evidence.


00:17:03.422 --> 00:17:05.390
- We have evidence.
- That is not admissible.


00:17:05.491 --> 00:17:08.722
The search warrant gave them the right
to search the house not the car.


00:17:08.827 --> 00:17:10.158
- He's right.
- Your Honor...


00:17:10.262 --> 00:17:12.787
The evidence of the drugs is inadmissible.


00:17:12.898 --> 00:17:15.958
In that case, Your Honor, we immediately
ask that all the charges be dropped


00:17:16.068 --> 00:17:17.695
and that the case be dismissed
with prejudice.


00:17:17.803 --> 00:17:20.533
Your Honor, we need to get him
out of the neighborhood.


00:17:20.639 --> 00:17:22.732
Then your officers
should have been more careful.


00:17:22.841 --> 00:17:26.402
- Where is your eyewitness?
- He has intimidated the entire community.


00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:28.844
Then your office
has its work cut out for them.


00:17:28.947 --> 00:17:31.245
I'm dismissing all the charges.


00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.749
Adjourned.


00:17:37.056 --> 00:17:38.956
They can't hold me, baby.


00:17:40.392 --> 00:17:41.825
- You're the man.
- Thank you.


00:17:41.927 --> 00:17:45.090
You want some pizza?
All right, I'm gonna bring some for you.


00:17:45.197 --> 00:17:47.062
All right, I'll there soon.


00:17:47.166 --> 00:17:48.690
I love you.


00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:55.870
- Well, do you see this?
- Yeah, I see it.


00:17:57.176 --> 00:17:58.473
I see it.


00:17:58.577 --> 00:18:00.511
You looking like a little massa boy.


00:18:00.612 --> 00:18:03.103
Wow. So, you had to get yourself
another job, huh?


00:18:03.215 --> 00:18:05.775
Yeah, I know feeding them girls
ain't easy, huh?


00:18:05.884 --> 00:18:08.819
Here. Let me help you out.
Let me see what I got in here.


00:18:08.921 --> 00:18:11.321
Oh, look at that. Here. Take it.


00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:12.913
- Stop it.
- Take it.


00:18:13.025 --> 00:18:15.289
Oh, so, what, you Mr. Do the Right Thing?


00:18:15.394 --> 00:18:18.454
Oh, so, you don't want this money.
It's okay. I'll take it back.


00:18:18.564 --> 00:18:21.499
- You gonna leave me alone?
- What you gonna do, baby?


00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:25.763
You see that brother right there?


00:18:25.871 --> 00:18:30.001
If I even break a nail,
he will shut you down.


00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:32.407
And I'm coming for my daughters.


00:18:33.145 --> 00:18:37.172
You don't even want your kids. Huh?
Now, why would you do all this?


00:18:37.282 --> 00:18:41.082
You tried to turn my mama against me,
huh?


00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:45.316
You tried to turn my kids against me?
It ain't gonna happen, baby.


00:18:45.424 --> 00:18:49.155
Yeah, I'm gonna make your life hell,
little punk.


00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:52.788
Look at him, Joe. I think he getting mad.


00:18:52.898 --> 00:18:56.129
He ain't gonna do nothing.
He's so scared to go back to jail.


00:18:56.235 --> 00:18:59.170
Yeah. Go on, looking like a slave.


00:18:59.271 --> 00:19:02.104
Go on, son. Mosey on down.


00:19:02.207 --> 00:19:04.232
- Go on and drive the car.
- Come on, now, baby.


00:19:04.343 --> 00:19:06.573
Let Stepin Fetchit get back to work now.


