00:34:32.970 --> 00:34:35.029
with all that mess? You're gonna stop that.


00:34:35.139 --> 00:34:39.576
- I want my daddy.
- Well, you ain't going back to your daddy.


00:34:39.677 --> 00:34:41.975
- Why?
- Because I said so, that's why.


00:34:42.080 --> 00:34:44.571
You're gonna stay right here with me.


00:34:45.550 --> 00:34:46.983
And you're going...


00:34:47.085 --> 00:34:50.612
China, you gonna stop that whining.
China, get in there. Get in there.


00:34:50.721 --> 00:34:53.189
You gonna stay here with me.
You ain't going back to your daddy.


00:34:53.291 --> 00:34:56.658
Now you get in there
until you figure that out. Get in there.


00:34:58.463 --> 00:35:01.796
Lauryn, go in there with her.
Go talk to your sister.


00:35:04.268 --> 00:35:05.826
I gotta tell you something now.


00:35:05.937 --> 00:35:08.599
Y'all better be glad I know Jesus.


00:35:09.440 --> 00:35:11.465
How y'all get on my nerves.


00:35:58.523 --> 00:35:59.990
Really beautiful.


00:36:01.459 --> 00:36:05.020
Selling drugs right out here
in front of this holy place.


00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:09.058
Oh, my goodness.
You know what, they need to be stopped.


00:36:09.167 --> 00:36:13.103
Janice's son got caught selling at school,
he said he got it from him.


00:36:13.204 --> 00:36:17.038
He comes to school and recruits the kids.
Babies, Monty.


00:36:17.141 --> 00:36:18.904
And then he sends them to go sell it.


00:36:19.010 --> 00:36:21.843
You know, Monty, you really need to come
to this community meeting.


00:36:21.946 --> 00:36:24.312
Monty, a lot of people respect you
in this neighborhood.


00:36:24.415 --> 00:36:26.610
And they still remember.


00:36:26.717 --> 00:36:29.686
- You should come to one of the meetings.
- I know.


00:36:29.787 --> 00:36:33.245
I'm praying for you,
and for you to get your girls back.


00:36:34.225 --> 00:36:37.092
- I'll babysit any time I can.
- I'll babysit, too.


00:36:37.195 --> 00:36:41.222
Honey, the Devil never wins,
unless you don't fight.


00:36:41.332 --> 00:36:43.095
Yeah. You're right.


00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:46.102
- All right, well, I'll see y'all later.
- Okay, baby.


00:36:47.939 --> 00:36:50.533
I'm going back in for a piece of cake.


00:36:54.178 --> 00:36:58.137
Now, you know, baby. You're old enough
to understand some things. Okay?


00:36:58.249 --> 00:36:59.978
All right?


00:37:00.084 --> 00:37:05.147
Now, you ain't gonna just be
sitting around here living off of me.


00:37:05.256 --> 00:37:06.723
You got that?


00:37:08.125 --> 00:37:10.889
Hey, look at me while I'm talking to you.


00:37:11.462 --> 00:37:14.761
Look at me while I'm talking to you, I said.


00:37:14.865 --> 00:37:17.629
Don't you dare not look at me.


00:37:21.072 --> 00:37:23.870
- It's time for you to start your own hustle.
- No.


00:37:23.975 --> 00:37:25.602
What do you mean, "No"?


00:37:26.844 --> 00:37:28.402
- Are you telling me...
- I'm not a hustler.


00:37:28.512 --> 00:37:31.709
No, you gonna be
whatever I tell you you gonna be.


00:37:31.816 --> 00:37:34.979
I'm trying to teach you how never
to be broke another day in your life.


00:37:35.086 --> 00:37:37.748
The number one rule to the game


00:37:37.855 --> 00:37:40.619
is never get caught.


00:37:41.659 --> 00:37:43.058
You got that?


00:37:47.732 --> 00:37:49.927
Now, I'm about to go get a drink.


00:37:50.768 --> 00:37:52.235
You want one?


00:37:57.675 --> 00:38:00.337
Willie's Garage. Can I help you?


00:38:00.444 --> 00:38:03.607
- Hold on. Monty, telephone.
- Yo.


00:38:09.954 --> 00:38:11.012
Yeah.


00:38:12.957 --> 00:38:13.981
What?


00:38:17.628 --> 00:38:19.892
We called her mother
but no one answered.


00:38:19.997 --> 00:38:22.557
This kind of thing is frowned upon,
Mr. James.


00:38:23.501 --> 00:38:24.695
Yes, sir.


00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:28.662
Sisi, where did you get this from? Huh?


00:38:29.607 --> 00:38:32.440
- Go ahead and answer me.
- Joe.


00:38:32.543 --> 00:38:33.703
Joe gave you this?


00:38:33.811 --> 00:38:36.541
- Who is Joe?
- Joe's her mother's boyfriend.


00:38:36.647 --> 00:38:38.877
What is wrong with you, Sisi?


00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:42.111
- Did you lose your mind?
- I don't want you to die.


00:38:42.219 --> 00:38:43.948
What are you talking about?


00:38:44.055 --> 00:38:48.287
He said if I didn't do it, he was going
to get one of his boys to take you out.


00:38:48.392 --> 00:38:51.361
And Joe crazy, Daddy.
He'll do it. I know he will.


00:38:51.462 --> 00:38:52.759
It's okay.


00:38:53.631 --> 00:38:56.065
Hey, didn't I tell you not to call him?
These are my kids.


00:38:56.167 --> 00:38:58.567
- Please.
- He has no right to my kids.


00:38:58.669 --> 00:39:00.603
Did you give this to my daughter to sell?


00:39:00.705 --> 00:39:02.536
- Is this punk talking to me?
- No, I don't think so.


00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:04.232
I'll take that as a yes. Look, man...


00:39:04.342 --> 00:39:05.934
Daddy!


00:39:08.446 --> 00:39:09.640
Look at him, you git.


00:39:09.747 --> 00:39:11.214
- Security, get up here.
- You wanna play?


00:39:11.315 --> 00:39:14.216
- Daddy!
- Now. Right away, to the Principal's office.


00:39:14.318 --> 00:39:16.309
- Let him go!
- I run this, man.


00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:18.388
Ain't nothing you can do about it.
These are my streets.


00:39:18.489 --> 00:39:19.581
It's okay, baby.


00:39:19.690 --> 00:39:22.215
Do yourself a favor, Monty, live.


00:39:22.326 --> 00:39:25.887
'Cause if you keep coming at me
the way you coming at me,


00:39:25.996 --> 00:39:29.329
we won't need a custody hearing.
You heard me?


00:39:29.433 --> 00:39:31.458
- Stop it, Sierra.
- Let go. Come here.


00:39:32.036 --> 00:39:34.903
Daddy's all right. Daddy's all right.


00:39:35.005 --> 00:39:37.565
- Daddy, please, can we go with you?
- Sierra, come on.


00:39:37.675 --> 00:39:38.767
- Sierra.
- Please.


00:39:38.876 --> 00:39:41.470
It's gonna be all right.
It's gonna be all right.


00:39:41.579 --> 00:39:43.843
- Sierra, come on.
- Let me go!


00:39:43.948 --> 00:39:45.848
Stop it. Both of you.


00:39:46.851 --> 00:39:49.285
- Stop grabbing her like that.
- What you doing, Sierra?


00:39:49.387 --> 00:39:51.355
It's gonna be all right, Sisi. All right?


00:39:51.455 --> 00:39:53.923
Why you gotta come up in here...


00:39:54.024 --> 00:39:55.582
If you come up in front of me again,


00:39:55.726 --> 00:39:58.854
I swear to God, you'll never see
another daylight in your life.


00:40:19.984 --> 00:40:21.611
- Morning.
- Hi.


00:40:24.255 --> 00:40:25.552
Excuse me.


00:40:27.057 --> 00:40:29.025
...and your 8:00 appointment's all set.
- Okay.


00:40:29.126 --> 00:40:30.184
Mr. Farnberg called.


00:40:30.294 --> 00:40:33.457
Oh, and I was able to reschedule
your hair appointment for next Tuesday.


00:40:33.564 --> 00:40:34.963
Also...


00:40:35.065 --> 00:40:37.863
- Hey, what are you doing in here?
- I needed to talk to you.


00:40:37.968 --> 00:40:39.959
That's what I was trying to tell you.
Mr. James is here.


00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:42.300
Yeah, obviously.
Did you just let him in my office?


00:40:42.406 --> 00:40:44.966
Well, he said he's here to drive you home.


00:40:45.075 --> 00:40:47.509
- Call security.
- No, you ain't gotta call security.


00:40:47.611 --> 00:40:49.977
I don't know what I was thinking
coming here talking to you.


00:40:50.080 --> 00:40:52.071
I'll just leave. I'm going.


00:40:52.183 --> 00:40:54.151
What do you want from me?


00:40:55.586 --> 00:40:58.054
I gotta talk to you about my kids.


00:41:02.226 --> 00:41:05.457
- Maya, can you give us a second, please?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:41:08.766 --> 00:41:11.462
I gotta get my girls back.


00:41:11.602 --> 00:41:14.127
Okay, what you need
is a family law attorney.


00:41:14.238 --> 00:41:16.502
Okay? And if you can't afford one,
the court will appoint one.


00:41:16.607 --> 00:41:18.199
I can't walk in there with a public lawyer.


00:41:18.309 --> 00:41:20.300
Their mama's spending
a lot of money on a lawyer.


00:41:20.411 --> 00:41:23.346
And I need a bulldog like you. No offense.


00:41:24.381 --> 00:41:27.282
Look, our firm charges $500 an hour.
Can you afford that?


00:41:27.384 --> 00:41:29.852
- I got $1,200 to my name.
- Look, Mr...


00:41:29.954 --> 00:41:32.252
No, no, just call me Monty.
Look, sister, I'm trying to get...


00:41:32.356 --> 00:41:34.324
Typical. Typical.


00:41:34.425 --> 00:41:37.656
I thought more of you, but it's real
typical. I'm not your sister, okay?


00:41:37.761 --> 00:41:41.720
I don't appreciate you coming
into my office asking for favors,


00:41:41.832 --> 00:41:43.299
playing the race thing.


00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:45.129
It's sad and it's pathetic.


00:41:46.704 --> 00:41:49.138
- What are you getting out of this?
- What?


00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:51.333
Why do you want your daughters back
so badly?


00:41:51.442 --> 00:41:55.503
You getting a check for them
or some sort of government assistance?


00:41:55.613 --> 00:41:56.807
Go to hell.


00:41:56.914 --> 00:42:00.372
Well, that, my friend, is exactly
how you get what you want.


00:42:00.484 --> 00:42:04.614
Insult me. Great strategy.
I see why you're so successful.


00:42:05.990 --> 00:42:07.821
Get a man. Get a life.


00:42:09.260 --> 00:42:10.557
Thank you.


00:42:17.301 --> 00:42:18.962
Excuse me, are any of you ladies
named Julia?


00:42:19.069 --> 00:42:20.161
- No.
- No.


00:42:20.271 --> 00:42:21.738
Sorry to bother you.


00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:28.773
Julia.


00:42:28.879 --> 00:42:30.608
- Christopher?
- Yes.


00:42:30.714 --> 00:42:32.807
- Please, call me Chris.
- Sure.


00:42:33.751 --> 00:42:35.685
- May I?
- Oh, please. Sorry.


00:42:42.059 --> 00:42:43.651
I'm sorry for staring.


00:42:43.761 --> 00:42:46.821
It's just that you're more beautiful
than your friend said.


00:42:46.931 --> 00:42:49.991
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:53.001
- So you're a lawyer?
- Yes, I am.


00:42:53.103 --> 00:42:55.628
- Me, too.
- Really? Wow.


00:42:55.739 --> 00:42:59.197
Mostly corporate stuff, tax stuff.
It's pretty boring. What about you?


00:42:59.310 --> 00:43:02.404
Our firm handles some criminal, some civil.


00:43:02.513 --> 00:43:05.107
- Okay. What firm?
- Rossmore & Blake.


00:43:05.215 --> 00:43:06.239
Oh.


00:43:07.851 --> 00:43:10.217
- What?
- I applied for a job there.


00:43:10.321 --> 00:43:12.619
They turned me down.


00:43:12.723 --> 00:43:15.214
Said that my resume
was a little bit shallow.


00:43:15.326 --> 00:43:17.556
That's what the old fart said.


00:43:18.796 --> 00:43:23.256
- What's he... How's he doing these days?
- He retired to Florida.


00:43:23.367 --> 00:43:27.235
- Oh, you keep up with him?
- He's my father, the fart.


00:43:29.773 --> 00:43:31.468
Check, please.


00:43:32.209 --> 00:43:35.372
- I'm sorry. That was embarrassing.
- Don't worry about it.


00:43:35.479 --> 00:43:38.744
He can be a little tough on people
he doesn't know that well.


00:43:38.849 --> 00:43:41.613
Oh, it must be big wingtips to fill.


00:43:41.719 --> 00:43:44.688
Actually I try to fill my own stilettos.


00:43:45.823 --> 00:43:48.621
Touché. And I will try to keep
my foot out of my mouth


00:43:48.726 --> 00:43:50.091
for the rest of this conversation.


00:43:50.194 --> 00:43:52.321
It's cute. You should leave it there.


00:43:52.429 --> 00:43:55.728
- Well, if it's what the lady likes, then I will.
- Oh, I like.


00:43:56.367 --> 00:44:01.031
- Would you like anything to drink?
- A latte would be great.


00:44:01.138 --> 00:44:03.072
Okay. Coming right up.


00:44:07.544 --> 00:44:08.841
Thank you, Jesus.


00:44:12.750 --> 00:44:14.980
So, I had an amazing time.


00:44:15.085 --> 00:44:18.680
This was one of the best dates
I've ever been on.


00:44:18.789 --> 00:44:19.983
Me, too.


00:44:20.624 --> 00:44:24.082
- I would like to see you again.
- Yeah? I'd like that.


00:44:27.631 --> 00:44:29.758
Who the hell is this, Chris?


00:44:35.005 --> 00:44:36.734
This is...


00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:38.205
Baby, you were supposed...


00:44:38.308 --> 00:44:41.766
- Who are you?
- I was just saying goodbye, ma'am.


00:44:41.879 --> 00:44:45.542
Yeah, you better go, slut.
You see, right now, this is his family.


00:44:46.216 --> 00:44:49.151
- Get away from my daddy, tramp.
- Junior!


00:44:49.253 --> 00:44:51.744
Excuse me, you're trying
to be playing player, huh?


00:44:51.855 --> 00:44:55.814
Where is your wedding ring?
That is so tired. Get into the car.


00:45:00.931 --> 00:45:03.764
- Where's your lawyer?
- Sir, I can't afford one.


00:45:03.867 --> 00:45:06.165
But I do have all my paperwork,
Your Honor.


00:45:06.270 --> 00:45:09.501
- Are you ready to begin?
- Yes, sir.


00:45:10.374 --> 00:45:12.604
- My kids were taken for...
- The court is aware of that,


00:45:12.710 --> 00:45:15.270
but first I'd like to hear about
the incident that happened at school.


00:45:15.379 --> 00:45:18.109
Your Honor, he gave my daughter weed
to sell in school


00:45:18.215 --> 00:45:19.614
so, you know, I had to handle that.


00:45:19.717 --> 00:45:22.880
Mr. James has no evidence
to support that allegation.


00:45:22.986 --> 00:45:25.580
However, we have documentation
that demonstrates


00:45:25.689 --> 00:45:28.817
that Mr. James has a history
of violent behavior.


00:45:28.926 --> 00:45:31.690
Your Honor, look, I'm caught between
a rock and a hard place here.


00:45:31.795 --> 00:45:34.593
You know, the courts won't help me.
My daughters are living with this man.


00:45:34.698 --> 00:45:36.290
You know,
what am I supposed to do right here?


00:45:36.400 --> 00:45:40.097
Your Honor, not only are we requesting
full custody with no visitation,


00:45:40.204 --> 00:45:42.934
but also a restraining order
against Mr. James.


00:45:43.040 --> 00:45:45.133
He assaulted my client
and threatened bodily injury.


00:45:45.242 --> 00:45:47.369
You Honor, this man
is giving drugs to my kids.


00:45:47.478 --> 00:45:49.378
- What proof of that do you have?
- Absolutely none.


00:45:49.480 --> 00:45:51.744
- Your Honor.
- Ms. Rossmore?


00:45:51.849 --> 00:45:54.181
I'll be representing Mr. James.


00:45:54.284 --> 00:45:56.582
I'd like to request a continuance
at this time


00:45:56.687 --> 00:45:57.984
so I might be brought up to speed.


00:45:58.088 --> 00:46:01.717
Your Honor, this has gone on long enough.
My client is ready to put this behind her.


00:46:01.825 --> 00:46:04.089
Perhaps counsel might want
to remind his client


00:46:04.194 --> 00:46:06.822
that in family court it's not
what's best for the parent,


00:46:06.930 --> 00:46:08.955
but rather what's
in the best interest of the child.


00:46:09.066 --> 00:46:10.727
That being said,


00:46:10.834 --> 00:46:13.496
I think these children
need effective counsel.


00:46:13.604 --> 00:46:17.836
Ms. Rossmore, you are appointed
by the court as guardian for the children.


00:46:17.941 --> 00:46:21.604
When I hear this case on the reset date,
I want evidence,


00:46:21.712 --> 00:46:25.375
not just accusations and speculation.


00:46:25.482 --> 00:46:27.245
This case is continued for 30 days.


00:46:27.351 --> 00:46:29.342
Your Honor,
during that time we'd like to request


00:46:29.453 --> 00:46:30.818
full custody be granted to the father.


00:46:30.921 --> 00:46:32.616
You're pushing your luck.


00:46:32.723 --> 00:46:34.714
Full custody remains with the mother.


00:46:34.825 --> 00:46:38.226
Father will have visitation one day a week.
Adjourned.


00:46:41.732 --> 00:46:44.633
You have really interesting taste in women.


00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:49.496
No, that's not the girl I met in high school.


00:46:49.606 --> 00:46:50.868
Nope, she's changed.


00:46:50.974 --> 00:46:54.671
I think the hood has a way of bringing out
the best and the worst in people.


00:46:54.778 --> 00:46:57.804
That's not just the hood, Monty. That's life.


00:46:57.915 --> 00:46:59.883
Yeah, maybe you're right.


00:46:59.983 --> 00:47:02.781
We had big dreams, though. Big dreams.


00:47:02.886 --> 00:47:05.252
Then I guess, you know, reality set in.


00:47:05.355 --> 00:47:08.415
Really? What kind of dreams did you have?


00:47:08.525 --> 00:47:11.961
I'm a mechanic and, you know,
I wanted to open my own shop.


00:47:12.062 --> 00:47:14.656
I'm good with cars, you know.
So that's my hustle.


00:47:14.765 --> 00:47:16.528
You should open that shop one day.


00:47:16.633 --> 00:47:20.000
Well, I had to use the money
that I had saved on my kids.


00:47:20.103 --> 00:47:22.071
- Oh.
- It was worth it, though.


00:47:22.172 --> 00:47:23.867
You know, I think that parents sometimes,


00:47:23.974 --> 00:47:27.603
they gotta give up their dreams
so their kids can have one.


00:47:32.716 --> 00:47:34.183
Thank you.


00:47:34.518 --> 00:47:36.452
- Thank you so much...
- All right.


00:47:36.553 --> 00:47:38.783
...for giving me hope. Thank you.


00:47:41.291 --> 00:47:42.918
Great. Cool. Okay.


00:47:50.067 --> 00:47:53.332
Come by tomorrow evening after work. We're
gonna have to do all this after-hours.


00:47:53.437 --> 00:47:55.200
- Okay.
- And if you could bring any receipt


00:47:55.305 --> 00:47:58.570
that pertains to the kids' expenses
or anything else you can possibly think of


00:47:58.675 --> 00:48:00.905
- that can help us win the case.
- Thank you.


00:48:09.386 --> 00:48:11.115
No, no, no. This needs to be addressed.


00:48:11.221 --> 00:48:13.815
He is the councilman.
He needs to know what the real issues are.


00:48:13.924 --> 00:48:16.017
You the one we elected.
You supposed to do something.


00:48:16.126 --> 00:48:17.388
- That's what.
- That's right.


00:48:17.494 --> 00:48:21.123
Quiet, quiet, please.
One at a time. One at a time.


00:48:21.231 --> 00:48:22.892
Yes, you, ma'am.


00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:27.369
I'm scared to go to the mailbox on
the first because they be watching me.


00:48:30.240 --> 00:48:31.502
Yes, sir.


00:48:32.209 --> 00:48:35.610
That Joe boy's been selling drugs
on this block for years.


00:48:35.712 --> 00:48:39.011
- Why haven't you called the police?
- What good would that do?


00:48:39.116 --> 00:48:42.643
He's been arrested five times
and he keeps coming back.


00:48:43.420 --> 00:48:46.116
- You gotta do something.
- That's right.


00:48:46.223 --> 00:48:48.555
What did I miss?


00:48:48.659 --> 00:48:51.093
More of the same. Still complaining.


00:48:51.194 --> 00:48:54.357
Let me tell you why
he's gonna keep getting off.


00:48:54.464 --> 00:48:58.696
Because none of you in this neighborhood
will testify against him.


00:49:01.872 --> 00:49:06.070
What if we did?
I mean, what if we did testify?


00:49:06.176 --> 00:49:08.041
Who's gonna protect us?


00:49:10.614 --> 00:49:15.347
Police don't come when you call them
in this neighborhood half the time.


00:49:15.452 --> 00:49:17.647
- May I say something, please?
- Yes, sir.


00:49:17.754 --> 00:49:20.723
I've been in this neighborhood
for almost 67 years.


00:49:20.824 --> 00:49:25.454
I've watched Dr. King walk this very street
to go to the barbershop.


00:49:25.562 --> 00:49:27.359
I remember Billie Holiday


